<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/</link><lastBuildDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:31:14 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>UN General Assembly enters second day with key speeches ahead</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/un-general-assembly-enters-second-day-with-key-speeches-ahead</link><description>
It’s Day Two of the United Nations General Assembly in New York, with a packed programme including speeches by Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian and Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky. Some of the biggest names in artificial intelligence will also address the UN Security Council. France 24’s Jessica Le Masurier is covering the gathering for us.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b1c2ae1c-b74d-11f1-a548-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-140159-140614-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b1c2ae1c-b74d-11f1-a548-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-140159-140614-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b804ab54-b74d-11f1-bac6-f70b2fc2239a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:10:45 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel denounces Macron's UN remarks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israel-denounces-macron-s-un-remarks</link><description>
Israeli officials have hit back at French President Emmanuel Macron after he criticised Israel’s conduct in the occupied West Bank during his address to the UN General Assembly. But while Macron used strong words against Israel, France allowed Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu’s plane to fly through French airspace on its way to New York, despite an ICC arrest warrant against him. Delano D’Souza reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7f9be0b0-b744-11f1-92a6-833f01c30b8b/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-130719-130913-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7f9be0b0-b744-11f1-92a6-833f01c30b8b/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-130719-130913-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8572b75c-b744-11f1-9d71-cd03806d7a8a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 11:56:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US President warns Tehran at UN but says talks ongoing</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-president-warns-tehran-at-un-but-says-talks-ongoing</link><description>
The day began with Donald Trump threatening to annihilate Iran but ended with a three-hour meeting between US and Iranian mediators, which Trump described as “very good.” Trump also held a high-level meeting with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky, with both sides saying they wanted the war in Ukraine to end before winter. Today, as the UN General Assembly continues, Zelensky and Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian are among those expected to address the assembly, as world leaders seek ways to end the two conflicts dominating international politics. France 24 International Affairs Editor Kethevane Gorjestani shares further insights.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4f81f8c8-b73b-11f1-9bbb-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-120230-120511-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4f81f8c8-b73b-11f1-9bbb-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-120230-120511-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">55615c0c-b73b-11f1-9c18-79ae88c1a4dc</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:46:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel blasts ‘grotesque absurdity’ of Macron’s UN remarks on West Bank</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-israel-blasts-grotesque-absurdity-of-macron-s-un-remarks-on-west-bank</link><description>
The Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's office on Wednesday issued a stinging rebuke to French President Emmanuel Macron's UN speech denouncing settler violence against Palestinians in the West Bank. Macron's remarks that "Hamas has never struck in the West Bank" was a "grotesque absurdity", said the statement.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b473bf6c-9d84-11f1-a6cf-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-10T111823Z-2133718736-RC2IULATYH0L-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-GAZA-PLAN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b473bf6c-9d84-11f1-a6cf-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-10T111823Z-2133718736-RC2IULATYH0L-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-GAZA-PLAN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">18e616ae-b728-11f1-9937-cf792c3070f5</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 08:41:50 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b473bf6c-9d84-11f1-a6cf-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-10T111823Z-2133718736-RC2IULATYH0L-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-GAZA-PLAN.jpg">© Ronen Zvulun, Reuters (File)</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US President Trump threatens "annihilation" of Iran despite successful talks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-president-trump-threatens-annihilation-of-iran-despite-successful-talks</link><description>
The day began with Donald Trump threatening to annihilate Iran but ended with a three-hour meeting between US and Iranian mediators, which Trump described as “very good.” Trump also held a high-level meeting with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky, with both sides saying they wanted the war in Ukraine to end before winter. Today, as the UN General Assembly continues, Zelensky and Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian are among those expected to address the assembly, as world leaders seek ways to end the two conflicts dominating international politics. First, Morgan Ayre reports on the latest developments in the Middle East.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ef5e96b4-b725-11f1-9742-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-090239-090427-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ef5e96b4-b725-11f1-9742-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-090239-090427-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f5e239f0-b725-11f1-a102-f71ab3b91949</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 08:22:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>AI risks, Iran war dominate agenda at UN</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-ai-risks-iran-war-to-take-center-stage-at-un</link><description>
France convenes a UN Security Council meeting Wednesday on artificial intelligence (AI) and international security, which includes briefings by leading industry figures, including the heads of OpenAI and Anthropic. The meeting comes as world leaders jostle over how to address the risks of the new technology. On the second day of the UN General Assembly, the Iran war is also set to dominate the agenda. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/57d4dafa-86e8-11f1-a7c3-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AFP-20260723-C3244N4-v1-MidRes-DebateBetweenCandidatesForUnSecretaryGeneralPost.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/57d4dafa-86e8-11f1-a7c3-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AFP-20260723-C3244N4-v1-MidRes-DebateBetweenCandidatesForUnSecretaryGeneralPost.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b2e4ad38-b70f-11f1-8b4a-75de2f89a542</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 05:29:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/57d4dafa-86e8-11f1-a7c3-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AFP-20260723-C3244N4-v1-MidRes-DebateBetweenCandidatesForUnSecretaryGeneralPost.jpg">© Leonardo Munoz, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Iran: Trump believes in an agreement after US midterms</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-iran-trump-believes-in-an-agreement-after-us-midterms</link><description>
US President Donald Trump told the United Nations General Assembly on Tuesday that he would have to decide whether to “annihilate” Iran if Tehran fails to reach a deal to end the war in the Middle East.
 
He added that he believed an agreement was possible after the US midterm elections in November.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e8874df6-b6a1-11f1-939f-d382746d948a/w:1024/p:16x9/Trump-onu.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e8874df6-b6a1-11f1-939f-d382746d948a/w:1024/p:16x9/Trump-onu.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0e98a306-b6a1-11f1-9554-97e461cbcfd6</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 16:17:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Trump says envoys Witkoff, Kushner met with mediators on potential Iran deal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260922-middle-east-live-yemen-fighting-escalates-as-trump-heads-to-un</link><description>
US President Donald Trump on Tuesday said ‌special envoys ‌Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner had met ‌with mediators on a possible deal to end the US war against Iran. Trump earlier threatened to "annihilate the Islamic Republic" if Tehran didn’t reach a peace deal with Washington in his UN General Assembly speech. Read about the day’s events as they unfolded on our liveblog. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/418cfcc0-b698-11f1-84e6-d382746d948a/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26265533113659.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/418cfcc0-b698-11f1-84e6-d382746d948a/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26265533113659.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">862bd6dc-b637-11f1-a4b2-b1db43887cfa</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 03:41:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/418cfcc0-b698-11f1-84e6-d382746d948a/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26265533113659.jpg">© Heather Khalifa, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Saudi Arabia left without US help against Houthis</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/saudi-arabia-left-without-us-help-against-houthis</link><description>
Saudi Arabia is weighing Washington’s refusal to help fend off Houthi attacks after Riyadh requested US assistance, despite the two countries being longstanding allies and President Donald Trump and his family maintaining close personal ties with Saudi leaders. France 24 International affairs commentator Douglas Herbert shares further details on this alliance.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/05396212-b5cc-11f1-ae0b-d5a6f2570fbe/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260921-160645-161307-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/05396212-b5cc-11f1-ae0b-d5a6f2570fbe/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260921-160645-161307-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0a898152-b5cc-11f1-96e8-8756c005b286</guid><pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 14:57:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Two tankers hit by 'unknown projectile' or debris in Strait of Hormuz</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260921-projectile-hits-tanker-as-it-enters-the-strait-of-hormuz</link><description>
Two tankers were hit in the Strait of Hormuz on Monday by either an "unknown projectile" or debris, a maritime security agency said. United Kingdom Maritime Trade Operations added that at least two crew members were injured in the first incident, and both vessels will continue to their next port of call.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f53555d0-b5bf-11f1-acdf-e554abee39f5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26250323137076.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f53555d0-b5bf-11f1-acdf-e554abee39f5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26250323137076.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">515ed59e-b5bf-11f1-bfe2-bfc44b452264</guid><pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 14:03:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f53555d0-b5bf-11f1-acdf-e554abee39f5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26250323137076.jpg">©  Vahid Salemi, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>West Bank: Israeli settler, Palestinian killed in latest violence</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/west-bank-israeli-settler-palestinian-killed-in-latest-violence</link><description>
Violence flared in the Israeli-occupied West Bank on Sunday, as Israeli forces arrested a suspected Palestinian gunman accused of killing an Israeli man. In a separate incident, Israeli soldiers killed a Palestinian driver who the military said had attempted to run them over. Nicholas Rushworth reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eeec1ca4-b5ba-11f1-abac-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260921-141854-142011-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eeec1ca4-b5ba-11f1-abac-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260921-141854-142011-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f40f9b02-b5ba-11f1-a271-7bd2a948b1ca</guid><pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 12:58:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israeli settler and Palestinian driver killed in West Bank shootings</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260920-israeli-settler-and-palestinian-driver-killed-in-west-bank-shootings</link><description>
A suspected Palestinian gunman on Sunday shot dead an Israeli man near a West Bank settlement, according to Israeli officials. The gunman was located at a Ramallah hospital and arrested, police said. Elsewhere in the West Bank, Israeli soldiers killed a Palestinian motorist who the military said was attempting to run them over. The flare up in violence came on the eve of the Jewish holy day of Yom Kippur. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/95da504c-b504-11f1-bc3f-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26263426242066.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/95da504c-b504-11f1-bc3f-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26263426242066.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bfa79150-b504-11f1-829e-c100d0797634</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 15:30:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/95da504c-b504-11f1-bc3f-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26263426242066.jpg">© Mahmoud Illean, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>An Israeli settler and a Palestinian driver killed in West Bank shootings</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/an-israeli-settler-and-a-palestinian-driver-killed-in-west-bank-shootings</link><description>
An Israeli settler has been fatally shot in the occupied West Bank, while Israel's military said it killed a man who attempted to ram his vehicle into troops elsewhere in the Palestinian territory. The news came as violence in the West Bank is escalating at a very rapid pace. “All Israeli military authorities involved with the West Bank have been warning the Israeli government that the situation is basically out of control”, explains FRANCE 24 correspondent Noga Tarnopolsky.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/420fc5b2-b4fc-11f1-8b03-9f514b90f153/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260920-150528-150741-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/420fc5b2-b4fc-11f1-8b03-9f514b90f153/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260920-150528-150741-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4722a830-b4fc-11f1-82b6-616b3c2ec8c7</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 14:34:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Iran closes French language centre in Tehran for ‘illegal acts’</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260920-iran-closes-french-language-centre-in-tehran-for-illegal-acts</link><description>
Iranian authorities on Sunday shut down the French Language Centre (CLF) in Tehran, alleging the French embassy-linked institute conducted "illegal acts that violated diplomatic conventions" and "abused its status as a language training facility". France has vowed to take "appropriate measures" in response.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d7627854-b4f1-11f1-a6d1-0730212ba17f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26258653383251.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d7627854-b4f1-11f1-a6d1-0730212ba17f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26258653383251.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e616cd3e-b4f4-11f1-8e86-3594b01563a8</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 13:46:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d7627854-b4f1-11f1-a6d1-0730212ba17f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26258653383251.jpg">© Vahid Salemi, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>The week in pictures: Syria protests, Céline Dion on stage and Quito wildfires</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260920-the-week-in-pictures-syria-protests-c%C3%A9line-dion-on-stage-and-quito-wildfires</link><description>
From protests against rising fuel prices in Syria to Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney’s EU charm offensive to Quito’s wildfires and Céline Dion’s return to the stage, FRANCE 24 looks back at the week's most striking pictures.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edae22ca-b343-11f1-8e1c-2b7cd267a8ec/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26259483265880.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edae22ca-b343-11f1-8e1c-2b7cd267a8ec/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26259483265880.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">74641fb4-b4dd-11f1-a404-1188b0c6eb5d</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 13:15:57 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edae22ca-b343-11f1-8e1c-2b7cd267a8ec/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26259483265880.jpg">© Baderkhan Ahmad, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Houthi attacks and no Western support: What are Saudi Arabia's options ?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/houthi-attacks-and-no-western-support-what-are-saudi-arabia-s-options</link><description>
The US has warned that fighting between Saudi Arabia and Iran-backed Houthis could rapidly escalate. It comes after a missile attack targeted Riyadh for the first time since the Yemen conflict resumed. The Houthis' lightning offensive seized swathes of Yemeni territory in recent weeks and has left hundreds dead. In the face of such attacks and with no support from its American ally, what are Saudi Arabia’s options?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5c423ba-b42e-11f1-9171-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T114800Z-1100229945-RC28MNAOL58F-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-YEMEN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5c423ba-b42e-11f1-9171-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T114800Z-1100229945-RC28MNAOL58F-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-YEMEN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cb76ca76-b4ed-11f1-a8aa-071222e1b868</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 12:24:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'NAZA' documentary about Gaza war sparks political storm in Israel</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/naza-documentary-about-gaza-war-sparks-political-storm-in-israel</link><description>
The Israeli filmmakers behind the documentary NAZA may have received a standing ovation at the Venice film festival, they have been facing violent threats to their lives and citizenship at home in Israel. A month ahead of crucial elections, the film profiles anonymous military sources who speak about the widespread killing of civilians in Gaza. Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said he intends to introduce legislation aimed at revoking the citizenship of people who "defame IDF soldiers". Details by Shirli Sitbon, FRANCE 24 international affairs editor.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd909d7e-b4ec-11f1-8bfb-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260920-133404-134124-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd909d7e-b4ec-11f1-8bfb-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260920-133404-134124-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d3300ac6-b4ec-11f1-bc19-e91039182cf6</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 12:22:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Why doesn't the US intervene to defend Saudi Arabia against the Houthis?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/why-doesn-t-the-us-intervene-to-defend-saudi-arabia-against-the-houthis</link><description>
The US cautioned against a rapidly escalating situation in Yemen after Houthi rebels carried out a missile attack on the Saudi capital. In recent weeks, the Iran backed militants have also seized large portions of Yemeni territory following clashes with Saudi-backed government forces. The US is a very close ally to Saudi Arabia. Yet, is visibly unwilling to intervene on its behalf – why? Details and analysis by H. A. Hellyer, senior fellow in geopolitics at the Royal United Institute in Cairo.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cce5cada-b4eb-11f1-98b6-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260920-130940-132125-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cce5cada-b4eb-11f1-98b6-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260920-130940-132125-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3855050a-b4ed-11f1-a96c-07e2d7a5aa9a</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 12:20:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Yemen's Houthis strike Saudi capital Riyadh for the first time</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-s-houthis-strike-saudi-capital-riyadh-for-the-first-time</link><description>
Fighting between Iran-backed Houthi rebels and Saudi Arabia continues to intensify. On Saturday morning, a fire broke out near Riyadh's main airport after Houthis said they launched missiles and drones at Saudi Arabia. On the ground in Yemen, Houthi rebels are pushing east in their fight against Saudi-backed government forces. Story by Caroline Baum.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/264babe8-b4d4-11f1-9455-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260920-080551-080719-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/264babe8-b4d4-11f1-9455-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260920-080551-080719-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2c53d6d2-b4d4-11f1-8661-553ba78fa9bc</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 09:38:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Black smoke seen near Riyadh amid air raid alerts in Saudi Arabia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/black-smoke-seen-near-riyadh-amid-air-raid-alerts-in-saudi-arabia</link><description>
⁠Flames and plumes of smoke ‌were ⁠seen ‌rising near ⁠Riyadh airport this afternoon with flights cancelled and delayed. This as fighting between Saudi-backed government forces and Iran-backed Houthi rebels has killed 48 people in recent hours. The rebels staged a lightning offensive this month, seizing swathes of territory in Yemen and launching a barrage of missiles and drones toward Saudi Arabia. Details and analysis by FRANCE 24 international affairs editor, Jamie Smith-Maillet.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6756645e-b43c-11f1-8e27-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260919-160101-160431-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6756645e-b43c-11f1-8e27-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260919-160101-160431-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6c85b75e-b43c-11f1-b045-e125042f2034</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 15:16:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Saudi Arabia says air defences intercepted Houthi ballistic missile targeting Riyadh</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260919-smoke-flames-seen-near-riyadh-airport-major-flight-disruptions-reported</link><description>
Saudi Arabia on Saturday confirmed that Yemen’s Houthi rebels tried to attack its capital with a ballistic missile, the first targeting of Riyadh since the escalation in fighting with the rebels. The confirmation came hours after the Houthis said they targeted "sensitive sites" in Saudi Arabia.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/40a51f4e-b423-11f1-bcd8-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T114802Z-1980126111-RC28MNAXZ2HR-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-YEMEN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/40a51f4e-b423-11f1-bcd8-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T114802Z-1980126111-RC28MNAXZ2HR-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-YEMEN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1ccc705c-b425-11f1-bb34-a7096373d88d</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:53:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/40a51f4e-b423-11f1-bcd8-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T114802Z-1980126111-RC28MNAXZ2HR-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-YEMEN.jpg">© Reuters via stringer</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel: 'NAZA' documentary sparks political storm</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260919-israel-naza-documentary-sparks-political-storm</link><description>
The documentary film 'NAZA', and its co-directors Yuval Abraham and Rachel Szor, are at the centre of a controversy in Israel.The film, which won an award at the Venice Film Festival, features anonymous Israeli sources accusing the military of intentionally killing numerous civilians in Gaza.Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said on Wednesday that he intended to "strip of their citizenship" those who "defame" the Israeli army.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/74111114-b426-11f1-9220-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/Vignette-RS.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/74111114-b426-11f1-9220-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/Vignette-RS.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9989a406-b426-11f1-ab3c-af9045de5f47</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:41:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>US fears wider Middle East escalation after Houthis attack Riyadh</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260919-us-fears-rapid-escalation-in-mideast-after-houthis-attack-riyadh</link><description>
The United States warned Saturday that fighting between Saudi Arabia and Iran-backed Houthi forces could “escalate rapidly” after a missile attack targeted Riyadh for the first time since the Yemen conflict resumed. The attack prompted US President Donald Trump to cut short a weekend at a secluded presidential complex in rural Maryland and return to the White House. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9940d6aa-b4ca-11f1-8af1-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T114756Z-1682804238-RC28MNAJERYX-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-YEMEN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9940d6aa-b4ca-11f1-8af1-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T114756Z-1682804238-RC28MNAJERYX-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-YEMEN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3d05ff42-b41a-11f1-a3af-9716bc3aebad</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 11:07:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9940d6aa-b4ca-11f1-8af1-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T114756Z-1682804238-RC28MNAJERYX-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-YEMEN.jpg">© Stringer, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>More than 112,000 displaced in Yemen as Houthis seize more ground</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/more-than-112-000-displaced-in-yemen-as-houthis-seize-more-ground</link><description>
Pro-Houthi demonstrations erupted in Yemen after Saudi Arabia accused the military group of targeting the Muslim holy site of Mecca. Story by Elitsa Gadeva.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a4e9a5ae-b407-11f1-b2e8-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-18T131305Z-414222399-RC2OLNAJ0IX0-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN-HOUTHIS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a4e9a5ae-b407-11f1-b2e8-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-18T131305Z-414222399-RC2OLNAJ0IX0-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN-HOUTHIS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3451f910-b405-11f1-9cb8-2d26d5c2c2ec</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 08:57:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The World This Week</category><title>AI: Silicon species or Trojan horse? Riyadh calling, Russia votes and the Ed Sheeran debate</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20260918-time-to-stop-suggesting-ai-is-conscious-riyadh-calling-saudi-s-hour-of-news-russian-elections</link><description>
This week, Saudi Arabia has turned to its allies for military support as Iran-backed Houthi rebels tighten their grip on Yemen’s Red Sea coast and the Bab al-Mandab shipping choke point, while drone attacks on the kingdom’s oil infrastructure deepen an emerging energy crisis. In Russia, voters head to the polls for a tightly controlled parliamentary election with little meaningful opposition, as Vladimir Putin insists there will be no new mobilisation. Meanwhile, warnings about the risks of AI are coming from inside the industry itself, with Microsoft’s AI chief Mustafa Suleyman warning against treating AI models like humans – and raising the prospect of a new “silicon species” competing with us for resources. Finally, in Britain, the royal family is back on the defensive as Earl Spencer’s new claims about Princess Diana’s funeral prompt an unusually pointed response from Buckingham Palace.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db7520f4-b393-11f1-a724-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/ANTHROPIC.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db7520f4-b393-11f1-a724-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/ANTHROPIC.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f2bd469a-b395-11f1-9f75-d9cba0bb1897</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 19:20:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>US approves $24.3 billion sale of 48 F-35 warplanes to Saudi Arabia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260918-us-approves-24-3-billion-sale-of-48-f-35-warplanes-to-saudi-arabia</link><description>
The United States on Thursday said it had approved a $24.3 billion sale of 48 F-35 stealth warplanes to Saudi Arabia. Israel has previously voiced concerns about Riyadh buying F-35s, despite a push to normalise relations.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b5501408-b328-11f1-82fe-1d1125ed9143/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T121806Z-145721001-RC2OFNAVWHNC-RTRMADP-3-NORWAY-ROYALS-KING-HARALD-FUNERAL.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b5501408-b328-11f1-82fe-1d1125ed9143/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T121806Z-145721001-RC2OFNAVWHNC-RTRMADP-3-NORWAY-ROYALS-KING-HARALD-FUNERAL.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0e13024a-b328-11f1-b171-f5081862f07e</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 06:29:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b5501408-b328-11f1-82fe-1d1125ed9143/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T121806Z-145721001-RC2OFNAVWHNC-RTRMADP-3-NORWAY-ROYALS-KING-HARALD-FUNERAL.jpg">© Claudia Greco, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump declines to back Saudi Arabia as US officials reportedly meet Iran-backed Houthis in Oman</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/trump-declines-to-back-saudi-arabia-as-us-officials-reportedly-meet-iran-backed-houthis-in-oman</link><description>
US officials met representatives of Yemen's Houthis in Oman over the weekend, five sources familiar with the matter said, days after the Iran-backed militia seized a strategic ​stretch of the ‌Red Sea coast in a sweeping offensive that routed Saudi-backed forces. U.S. ​President Donald Trump has so far rebuffed pleas from the Saudis for military support fighting the Houthis. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson reports from Washington.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e67af742-ae18-11f1-ae71-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7VR3NQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e67af742-ae18-11f1-ae71-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7VR3NQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6925b04e-b2c7-11f1-94b8-0bacc0414a65</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 18:47:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Stalemate' in Lebanon: Hezbollah justifies weapons, citing Israeli occupation and ongoing attacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/stalemate-in-lebanon-hezbollah-justifies-weapons-citing-israeli-occupation-and-ongoing-attacks</link><description>
Angela Diffley is pleased to welcome Dr Filippo Dionigi, Senior Lecturer in Politics and International Relations at the University of Bristol. According to Dr. Dionigi, the central obstacle to Hezbollah’s disarmament is not simply the military capacity of the Lebanese state, but the absence of a political settlement capable of making disarmament both legitimate and sustainable. While additional funding and weapons would strengthen the Lebanese Armed Forces, they will not resolve the fundamental political dilemma. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7dac3526-b2b6-11f1-a1e4-1d1125ed9143/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-151052-152026-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7dac3526-b2b6-11f1-a1e4-1d1125ed9143/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-151052-152026-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">83b316ce-b2b6-11f1-8566-3167f41fb792</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 18:44:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>'Sanctions won’t prevent us from doing our job' says ICC Prosecutor Mame Mandiaye Niang</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20260917-sanctions-won-t-prevent-us-from-doing-our-job-says-icc-prosecutor-mame-mandiaye-niang</link><description>
In this edition of Perspective, the acting Prosecutor of the International Criminal Court tells FRANCE 24 that the court is needed now more than ever to ensure there is no gap for impunity. Mame Mandiaye Niang says the court’s job is to step in if domestic justice systems fail. The Senegalese judge is at the centre of a storm amid sanctions put on the court by the US after its issuing of arrest warrants for Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and former Defence Minister Yoav Gallant over Israel’s actions in Gaza. He explained how the sanctions affect his daily life but says it won’t stop the court doing its job.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/332e1d38-b27b-11f1-8dd7-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/ANGL260917-0940-Live-CS0940.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/332e1d38-b27b-11f1-8dd7-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/ANGL260917-0940-Live-CS0940.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">42111864-b27b-11f1-8a60-a3ca3ffd93d4</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 16:02:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Stuart NORVAL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Gaza documentary 'NAZA' sparks political storm, threats against directors in Israel</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260917-gaza-documentary-naza-sparks-political-storm-in-israel</link><description>
The award-winning documentary "NAZA" featuring anonymous military sources speaking about Israel's mass killing of civilians in Gaza has sparked a political firestorm in Israel. The film's directors and their families have received a wave of threats, while Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu announced a plan for a bill aimed at revoking the citizenship of people who "defame IDF soldiers".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c69183f2-b2b8-11f1-a9f1-61f6f55d211c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26258555934130.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c69183f2-b2b8-11f1-a9f1-61f6f55d211c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26258555934130.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e73ee87c-b2ab-11f1-bad0-7d4ece9fee5a</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 15:24:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c69183f2-b2b8-11f1-a9f1-61f6f55d211c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26258555934130.jpg">© Ariel Schalit, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
